From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:48:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: give an X window made again its _NET_WM_USER_TIME.

A window mapped without being activated carries a _NET_WM_USER_TIME of 0,
which tells the window manager not to give it the focus nor put it on top
of the window that has it.  The value last set was remembered with the
window data and not set again when the X window was made anew for another
visual, so the new X window went without, and mutter put it above the
focused window when it was mapped: after a display change, the shadow of a
window at the back showed across the window in front.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 139afd2027aa8bbfca383c5790cd03c908cd60cf)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index c20680c2122..327fea8b991 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -2652,6 +2652,9 @@ static void destroy_whole_window( struct x11drv_win_data *data, BOOL already_des
     data->configure_serial = 0;
     data->net_wm_icon_serial = 0;
     data->reparenting = 0;
+    /* a window made again, for another visual, has no _NET_WM_USER_TIME: without one, one mapped
+     * without being activated is put on top of the focused window by the window manager */
+    data->user_time = -1;
 
     if (data->xic)
     {
